1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:03,970
Before coming to Yale, I worked in real estate investment funds,

2
00:00:03,970 --> 00:00:08,514
where I spent a lot of time evaluating development opportunities and building financial models.

3
00:00:08,514 --> 00:00:09,812
For my final project,

4
00:00:09,812 --> 00:00:13,707
I wanted to create something that could make that process more efficient.

5
00:00:13,707 --> 00:00:15,330
That's how TerraMind AI started.

6
00:00:15,730 --> 00:00:19,476
TerraMind helps users evaluate different types of real estate investments,

7
00:00:19,476 --> 00:00:22,473
from residential developments to commercial and industrial properties.

8
00:00:22,473 --> 00:00:25,469
The process starts with the property's basic information,

9
00:00:25,469 --> 00:00:29,590
which the platform uses to guide the rest of the analysis.

10
00:00:30,095 --> 00:00:35,492
One of the first steps is understanding what can actually be developed on a property.

11
00:00:35,492 --> 00:00:37,291
TerraMind can research development regulations,

12
00:00:37,291 --> 00:00:41,968
but it also allows users to provide their own information or upload documents,

13
00:00:41,968 --> 00:00:44,847
such as permits, contracts, or existing financial models,

14
00:00:44,847 --> 00:00:48,445
so the analysis can build on information they already have.

15
00:00:49,012 --> 00:00:52,854
The platform then connects development assumptions, construction costs, projected revenues,

16
00:00:52,854 --> 00:00:55,159
and financing into a financial model.

17
00:00:55,159 --> 00:00:58,617
Instead of asking users to estimate the final returns,

18
00:00:58,617 --> 00:01:01,307
TerraMind calculates them from the underlying assumptions.

19
00:01:01,307 --> 00:01:08,222
Users can also export the model to Excel to review or continue working on it outside the application.

20
00:01:10,986 --> 00:01:13,918
The feature I find most interesting is the chatbot.

21
00:01:13,918 --> 00:01:15,873
Instead of navigating through multiple spreadsheets,

22
00:01:15,873 --> 00:01:19,456
users can explain what they want to change in natural language.

23
00:01:19,706 --> 00:01:20,153
Here,

24
00:01:20,153 --> 00:01:28,637
a ten percent increase in construction costs raises the hard cost from 24,000 to 26,400 pesos per square meter,

25
00:01:28,637 --> 00:01:32,656
and the equity IRR falls from 24.9% to 21.2%.

26
00:01:32,906 --> 00:01:36,886
The assistant can update assumptions, incorporate more complex cash-flow schedules,

27
00:01:36,886 --> 00:01:40,866
and help users understand how those changes affect the investment.

28
00:01:50,432 --> 00:01:53,671
I also wanted to make the platform easier to use,

29
00:01:53,671 --> 00:01:57,882
so I added speech-to-text functionality. Users can dictate instructions instead of typing them.

30
00:01:57,882 --> 00:02:01,445
And because I eventually want this to be useful in Mexico,

31
00:02:01,445 --> 00:02:03,712
the application supports both English and Spanish.

32
00:02:04,112 --> 00:02:07,850
Another important objective was incorporating sustainability into investment decisions.

33
00:02:07,850 --> 00:02:12,420
TerraMind can help compare different improvements and evaluate their financial impact.

34
00:02:12,420 --> 00:02:16,573
The AI agents can also review the investment, identify risks,

35
00:02:16,573 --> 00:02:20,312
and suggest changes that could improve the project's performance.

36
00:02:20,821 --> 00:02:25,062
I also wanted TerraMind to be useful beyond the initial investment decision.

37
00:02:25,062 --> 00:02:30,011
Users can save projects, return to their analyses, and monitor how investments are performing.

38
00:02:30,011 --> 00:02:33,545
The platform supports individual accounts to keep project information separate,

39
00:02:33,545 --> 00:02:38,141
as well as guest access for someone who just wants to explore it.

40
00:02:38,521 --> 00:02:40,095
TerraMind is still a prototype,

41
00:02:40,095 --> 00:02:44,816
but it brings together several parts of real estate investing that are usually handled separately.

42
00:02:44,816 --> 00:02:49,538
I see it as a starting point for something I could continue developing after Yale,

43
00:02:49,538 --> 00:02:53,631
especially as I pursue my interest in real estate investment and sustainable development.
